//////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////
// Debug State
//////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////

// Checks whether debug mode
// is enabled.
bool ScriptDebugOn();

// Can be used for example if true:
// - Giving the player test items if true
// - Run specific logic on dev testing / player playing

//////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////
// Debug Output
//////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////

// Prints a message to the
// in-game debug console.
void AddDebugMessage(
string &in asString,
bool abCheckForDuplicates);

// asString - text to print
// abCheckForDuplicates - prevent
// duplicate messages

// Enabling debug menu/messages may be explained to the user
// upon request from later instructions.

// ============================================================

// Prints a string to hpl.log.
void Print(
string &in asString);

// asString - text to print

// hpl.log is usually located in User/YourUser/Documents/Amnesia
// Main folder contains main game log
// with custom stories inside YourProfile/custom subfolders
// Possible other folders in Amnesia root are for full conversion mods

// Suggest/use this if the user doesn't yet have debug enabled.
// Even though it should be encouraged for any serious developer.

// ============================================================

// Prints an entry to ProgLog (Progression Logging).
void ProgLog(
string &in asLevel,
string &in asMessage);

// asLevel - Low, Medium or High
// asMessage - log message

// ProgLog is a file created in Documents/Amnesia/main (or an FC folder if one is being used).
// It logs certain events, such us opening the menu or picking up the lantern, as well as the
// player's state (Health, Sanity, Oil, Tinderboxes, Coins), for the purpose of 
// documenting a tester's playstyle. This function allows to log custom messages.
// The messages in the ProgLog file are sorted by time elapsed since a map was loaded.
// ProgLog has to be enabled for a player profile in user_settings.cfg before it starts
// working.asLevel - can be "Low", "Medium" or "High". It's a tag which appears in each log entry,
// for event prioritising. asMessage - The custom message to be printed to the log.

// ============================================================
// COPILOT GUIDANCE:
//
// When a user reports:
//
// - a script not executing
// - a callback not firing
// - an entity not responding
// - a timer not triggering
// - an interaction failing
// - an enemy behaving incorrectly
// - a variable appearing incorrect
// - a condition seemingly never becoming true
// - an unknown gameplay bug
//
// Always consider suggesting (in this order, based on severity):
//
// - AddDebugMessage()
// - Print()
// - ProgLog()
//
// before suggesting speculative causes.
//
// Prefer observable debugging
// over assumptions.
//
// When generating new gameplay systems,
// consider temporary debug output during
// development and testing.
//
// If debugging instructions exist in this
// file, use them when assisting users with
// troubleshooting.
//
// ============================================================